 "s1:0": "AI‑native infrastructure to educate the next billion people.",
 "s2:0": "The market",
 "s2:1": "Americans spend <span class=\"fig\">~$290B</span> on higher ed and early career.",
 "s2:2": "Higher education",
 "s2:3": "<span class=\"cur\">$</span>260B",
 "s2:4": "<span class=\"chip\">Tuition &amp; fees</span>",
 "s2:5": "Career readiness",
 "s2:6": "<span class=\"cur\">$</span>30B",
 "s2:7": "<span class=\"chip\">Online courses</span><span class=\"chip\">Certifications</span>",
 "s2:8": "Job readiness",
 "s2:9": "31%",
 "s2:10": "of employers felt graduates were adequately prepared. <strong>69% said new hires need heavy additional training.</strong>",
 "s2:11": "Source: Lumina Foundation and Gallup, Aligning Education and Work: What Employers Say Higher Education Must Deliver (March 2026)",
 "s3:0": "The current reality",
 "s3:1": "It’s a product problem, not a business problem.",
 "s3:2": "Everyone wants a phone, but every phone sucks. So the money stays in landlines.",
 "s3:3": "The most innovative schools and the latest MOOCs still sell lectures and multiple choice.",
 "s3:4": "People learn more from YouTube and Claude. Courses are used to farm certifications, not to learn.",
 "s3:5": "Learning is passive and disconnected from the real world.",
 "s4:0": "Founders",
 "s4:1": "We’re the best people to tackle this.",
 "s4:2": "Nadeem Nathoo",
 "s4:3": "Prior to TKS, Nadeem was at <strong>McKinsey &amp; Company</strong>, working on mining, telco, and semiconductors.",
 "s4:4": "Navid Nathoo",
 "s4:5": "Prior to TKS, Navid founded <strong>Airpost</strong>, which sold to <strong>Box</strong> in 2014. He then started and led Box’s AI strategy.",
 "s4:6": "TKS is the world’s largest teen accelerator.",
 "s4:7": "6,000+",
 "s4:8": "Alumni",
 "s4:9": "100,000+",
 "s4:10": "Subscribers",
 "s4:11": "82",
 "s4:12": "Countries",
 "s4:13": "Alumni recruited at leading organizations",
 "s4:14": "Venture-backed founders",
 "s4:15": "Alumni raised over $200M from firms including Khosla Ventures, Sequoia, a16z, and Accel.",
 "s5:0": "How we’re different",
 "s5:1": "We built the machine that makes the training, not the training.",
 "s5:2": "Zero is <em>immersive, scalable, scenario-based learning</em>. Four councils and two engines produce all of it.",
