 "s6:0": "Technology · Content engines",
 "s6:1": "Two engines turn curriculum into product, on the fly.",
 "s6:2": "Training generation guild",
 "s6:3": "Any training, on any topic, generated the moment it’s needed.",
 "s6:4": "\n              <span class=\"fchip\">Tool simulations</span>\n              <span class=\"fchip\">Concept training</span>\n              <span class=\"fchip\">Workflow training</span>\n              <span class=\"fchip\">Communication training</span>\n              <span class=\"fchip\">Mini games</span>\n              <span class=\"fchip\">Co-worker training</span>\n            ",
 "s6:5": "Six of fifteen formats shown. Think YouTube, but generated for exactly what you need to learn next.",
 "s6:6": "Media &amp; production wing",
 "s6:7": "Every scenario ships with its own media, fully produced by agents.",
 "s6:8": "01",
 "s6:9": "Co-worker kick-off videos <span>that brief you like a real manager would.</span>",
 "s6:10": "02",
 "s6:11": "Intros and outros <span>for every stage of the scenario.</span>",
 "s6:12": "03",
 "s6:13": "A voice for every character <span>in the story you work inside.</span>",
 "s6:14": "Adding a job role is a generation run, not a production project. The catalog grows without growing the team.",
 "s7:0": "Technology · Proof &amp; placement",
 "s7:1": "We measure the work, then take it to market.",
 "s7:2": "Evaluation &amp; feedback",
 "s7:3": "Graded on evidence, not on answers.",
 "s7:4": "Every decision, message, and artifact a student produces is scored against the criteria the councils set, and the feedback lands while the work is still open.",
