 "s10:0": "Business model",
 "s10:1": "A credit subscription, priced like Claude.",
 "s10:2": "Starter",
 "s10:3": "Free",
 "s10:4": "10,000 credits",
 "s10:5": "Plus",
 "s10:6": "<span class=\"cur\">$</span>99",
 "s10:7": "20,000 credits / month",
 "s10:8": "Max",
 "s10:9": "<span class=\"cur\">$</span>199",
 "s10:10": "Unlimited (fair-use cap)",
 "s10:11": "Credits burn through usage · running out converts · top-ups $25 per 4,000",
 "s10:12": "P1",
 "s10:13": "Direct-to-consumer",
 "s10:14": "Subscription revenue first. Scale the base.",
 "s10:15": "P2",
 "s10:16": "Credentials &amp; certifications",
 "s10:17": "Upsell the existing base on CompTIA, AWS, and similar.",
 "s10:18": "P3",
 "s10:19": "Recruitment revenue",
 "s10:20": "Monetize direct hiring out of Zero.",
 "s11:0": "Go to market",
 "s11:1": "Three channels, one bridge from degree to employment.",
 "s11:2": "01",
 "s11:3": "College career departments",
 "s11:4": "Careers teams are measured on placement and have no product that delivers it. <strong>Handshake</strong> is the case study for how fast this channel adopts.",
 "s11:5": "02",
 "s11:6": "Paid and organic social",
 "s11:7": "Held to a <strong>3:1+ LTV to CAC</strong> target, with a UGC motion on top: students posting portfolios, projects, and co-worker interactions.",
 "s11:8": "03",
 "s11:9": "Product marketing",
 "s11:10": "Credit awards inside the product turn active students into the referral engine, paying for growth in the currency they already want.",
 "s12:0": "We’re building the world’s largest Human Capital company.",
 "s13:0": "Future ambition",
 "s13:1": "Human capital is a $5 trillion market.",
 "s13:2": "K–12, higher ed, recruitment, and corporate L&amp;D all sit on one shared foundation: developing, measuring, and deploying human capital.",
